course: dictionary
lesson: 4028
title: One word, three jobs: gauge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «Rainfall is measured with a rain gauge in millimetres.» Here a gauge is a tool. The words rain and millimetres are the clues: a gauge that measures rain is an instrument that shows an amount.
explain: Gauge can also be a doing word. «Gauge how someone feels» means judge or guess how they feel. No tool is involved. If the sentence has a person doing something, such as judging or guessing, gauge is probably a verb.
explain: Gauge can also mean the width or thickness of something, such as the thickness of a wire. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A gauge is an instrument that measures and shows an amount.
fact: Examples are a fuel gauge, a pressure gauge, a rain gauge and a tyre gauge.
fact: «Rainfall is measured with a rain gauge in millimetres.»
fact: As a verb, «to gauge» means to measure something exactly, or to judge or guess something, such as how far away it is.
fact: Gauge can also mean the width or thickness of something, like the distance between railway tracks.
exercise: «Rainfall is measured with a rain gauge in millimetres.» What is a rain gauge? | A cloud that holds the rain | A bucket for carrying water | A wind vane that shows the direction of the wind | *An instrument that measures and shows how much rain has fallen
exercise: «Tsunami warning centres use earthquake sensors and pressure gauges on the sea floor to warn coasts.» What does a pressure gauge do? | It measures the temperature of the water | *It measures and shows the pressure on the sea floor | It carries warnings to the coast
exercise: Sam wants to «gauge how far away the storm is». What does gauge mean here? | To buy something | To paint a picture | *To judge or guess
test: The fuel gauge in the car showed the tank was almost empty. What does the fuel gauge show? | The speed of the car | *The amount of fuel left in the tank | The number of passengers
test: Wire comes in different gauges, so a thin wire has a small gauge. What does gauge mean here? | How cold it is | *How thick or wide it is | How heavy it is | How it is painted
exam: Which sentence uses gauge as a verb? | The rain gauge sat on the lawn | The tyre gauge showed the air was low | *Mum tried to gauge how tired I was | The fuel gauge was empty
